# number of interfaces
 4
#
# !!!!!!!!!!!Each interface in the DSM model covered in the SEM box must be described here!!!!!!!!!!!!!
# Description of each interface:
# Each interface is represented as a structured 2D grid defined by the following parameters:
# - NXI, NETA: Number of grid points along the XI and ETA directions.
# - XI_MIN, ETA_MIN: Minimal XI and ETA coordinates (cubed-sphere or Cartesian system).
# - SPACING_XI, SPACING_ETA: Constant grid spacing in the XI and ETA directions.
# - Z coordinates: Grid heights/depths specified in a separate data file containing NXI x NETA points.
#
# Notes:
# - For SEM-DSM coupling (COUPLING_TYPE=1, 2, or 3), the coordinates (XI, ETA) are in the cubed-sphere system.
# - Use the tool `src/cubedsphere_topo/` to convert topography from (longitude, latitude) to (XI, ETA) format (see ../../step1_mesh_gen.sh).
# Interface 4: Represents the ICB
# SUPPRESS_UTM_PROJECTION  NXI  NETA  XI_MIN   ETA_MIN    SPACING_XI SPACING_ETA
 .true.                   300 300 -0.5        -0.5      0.015    0.015
# Data file containing Z coordinates for this interface
  topo_735km.dat
# Interface 3: Represents the ICB
# SUPPRESS_UTM_PROJECTION  NXI  NETA  XI_MIN   ETA_MIN    SPACING_XI SPACING_ETA
 .true.                   300 300 -0.5        -0.5      0.015    0.015
# Data file containing Z coordinates for this interface
 topo_660km.dat
# Interface 2: Represents the top of the mesh (surface topography)
 .true.                   300 300 0.d0        0.d0      0.03d0    0.03d0
 topo_25km.dat
# Interface 1: Represents the top of the mesh (surface topography)
 .true.                   300 300 0.d0        0.d0      0.03d0    0.03d0
 topo_top.dat
